{"pin":"BH05849","subcodes":[{"code":"BH05849","anchor":"","title":"Prayer for Ayyam-i-Ha","first_line":"My God, my Fire and my Light! The days which Thou hast named the Ayyam-i-Ha in Thy Book have begun","first_line_orig":"قل یا الهی و ناری و نوری قد دخلت الایام التی سمیتها بایام الهاء فی کتابک یا  ","language":"Ara","word_count":"170","notes":" \u003ca href=\"https://bahai-library.com/bahailib/1504.pdf#page=118\"\u003eMMAH.106\u003c/a\u003e,  \u003ca href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20070930181707/http://bahai-library.com/resources/leiden.list/leiden.list.html#462\"\u003eLL#462\u003c/a\u003e","full_text_parts":["*(The Intercalary Days, February 26 to March 1, inclusive, should be days of preparation for the Fast, days of hospitality, charity and the giving of presents.)\n\n\n\nMy God, my Fire and my Light!  The days which Thou hast named the Ayyám-i-Há¹ in Thy Book have begun, O Thou Who art the King of names, and the Fast which Thy most exalted Pen hath enjoined unto all who are in the kingdom of Thy creation to observe is approaching.  I entreat Thee, O my Lord, by these days and by all such as have during that period clung to the cord of Thy commandments, and laid hold on the handle of Thy precepts, to grant that unto every soul may be assigned a place within the precincts of Thy court, and a seat at the revelation of the splendors of the light of Thy countenance.\nThese, O my Lord, are Thy servants whom no corrupt inclination hath kept back","from what Thou didst send down in Thy Book.  They have bowed themselves before Thy Cause, and received Thy Book with such resolve as is born of Thee, and observed what Thou hadst prescribed unto them, and chosen to follow that which had been sent down by Thee.\nThou seest, O my Lord, how they have recognized and confessed whatsoever Thou hast revealed in Thy Scriptures.  Give them to drink, O my Lord, from the hands of Thy graciousness the waters of Thine eternity.  Write down, then, for them the recompense ordained for him that hath immersed himself in the ocean of Thy presence, and attained unto the choice wine of Thy meeting.\nI implore Thee, O Thou the King of kings and the Pitier of the downtrodden, to ordain for them the good of this world and of the world to come.  Write down for them, moreover, what none of Thy creatures hath","discovered, and number them with those who have circled round Thee, and who move about Thy throne in every world of Thy worlds.\nThou, truly, art the Almighty, the All-Knowing, the All-Informed.\n\n\n*1. The Days of Há, Intercalary Days."],"translations":[{"language":"ml","lang_name":"Malayalam"},{"language":"ru","lang_name":"Russian"},{"language":"bi","lang_name":"Bislama"},{"language":"es","lang_name":"Spanish"},{"language":"bg","lang_name":"Bulgarian"},{"language":"hi","lang_name":"Hindi"},{"language":"ro","lang_name":"Romanian"},{"language":"id","lang_name":"Indonesian"},{"language":"zh-Hant","lang_name":"Traditional Chinese"},{"language":"vi","lang_name":"Vietnamese"},{"language":"sv","lang_name":"Swedish"},{"language":"tl","lang_name":"Tagalog"},{"language":"uk","lang_name":"Ukrainian"},{"language":"ar","lang_name":"Arabic"},{"language":"fi","lang_name":"Finnish"},{"language":"iba","lang_name":"Iban"},{"language":"mt","lang_name":"Maltese"},{"language":"hy","lang_name":"Armenian"},{"language":"kl","lang_name":"Kalaallisut"},{"language":"mg","lang_name":"Malagasy"},{"language":"ja","lang_name":"Japanese"},{"language":"pt","lang_name":"Portuguese"},{"language":"mn","lang_name":"Mongolian"},{"language":"fa","lang_name":"Persian"},{"language":"kn","lang_name":"Kannada"},{"language":"da","lang_name":"Danish"},{"language":"fr","lang_name":"French"},{"language":"ms","lang_name":"Malay"},{"language":"sne","lang_name":"Bau Bidayuh"},{"language":"ta","lang_name":"Tamil"},{"language":"bn","lang_name":"Bengali"},{"language":"eo","lang_name":"Esperanto"},{"language":"ko","lang_name":"Korean"},{"language":"zh-Hans","lang_name":"Simplified Chinese"},{"languag